import json
from pathlib import Path
base=Path('src/content')
for name,count in [('extended-programs/ml',6),('extended-programs/fullstack',6),('extended-programs/leadership',4),('space',4)]:
 if len(json.loads((base/(name+'.json')).read_text())['modules'])!=count: raise SystemExit('One-time content migration already applied; edit JSON directly.')
def m(title,icon,summary,topics,tools,practice,deliverables,criteria):return dict(title=title,icon=icon,summary=summary,topics=topics.split('|'),tools=tools.split('|'),practice=practice,deliverables=deliverables.split('|'),criteria=criteria.split('|'))
def save(name,d): (base/(name+'.json')).write_text(json.dumps(d,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
d=json.loads((base/'extended-programs/ml.json').read_text());old=d['modules']
features=m('Feature engineering & reproducible pipelines','layers','Make the same transformations work reliably during training and prediction.','Missing-value strategies and missingness indicators|Categorical encoding, scaling and skewed distributions|Column-wise transformations and feature provenance|Train-only fitting and leakage checks|Pipeline persistence and feature-contract tests','pandas — inspect values and categories|ColumnTransformer and Pipeline — join transformations with estimators|pytest — test feature contracts and unseen-category behaviour','Build a reusable preprocessing pipeline for mixed numerical and categorical data. Introduce an unseen category and missing field, then document the intended prediction-time behaviour.','Feature dictionary with availability times|Reproducible preprocessing pipeline|Tests for missing and unfamiliar inputs','Fit learned transformations only on training folds|Explain what each feature means at prediction time|Keep validation data out of feature selection')
models=m('Regression, classification & model comparison','chart','Understand which model family is useful, and why its errors differ.','Linear and logistic regression, regularisation and decision boundaries|Decision trees, random forests and gradient boosting|Nearest neighbours and support-vector machines as comparison models|Bias–variance tradeoffs and learning curves|Probability estimates, thresholds and the cost of different errors','scikit-learn estimators — compare model families|DummyRegressor and DummyClassifier — establish simple baselines|Matplotlib — inspect residuals, learning curves and confusion matrices','Compare a linear model, a tree ensemble and a dummy baseline on the same fixed split. Explain a case where the most complex model is not the most useful choice.','Comparison table with identical evaluation conditions|Residual or error-slice analysis|A model-choice note with operational constraints','Use the same data split and metric definitions|Separate hyperparameter selection from final test evaluation|Explain errors and resource costs as well as headline scores')
time=m('Time-aware prediction & forecasting','clock','Respect the order in which information becomes available.','Forecast horizons and seasonal or lag features|Time-based splits and rolling validation|Naive and seasonal baselines|Delayed labels, missing periods and changing patterns|Prediction intervals as an introductory uncertainty topic','pandas datetime tools — align time-indexed observations|TimeSeriesSplit — run chronological validation|scikit-learn — compare lag-feature regression against a baseline','Forecast a sample daily demand series. Hold out the latest period, construct features using past data only and compare performance across busy and quiet intervals.','Forecast notebook and chronological split diagram|Baseline comparison by forecast horizon|Limitations note for sparse history and unexpected events','Never use future observations to construct past features|Evaluate on the horizon the proposed user needs|Avoid presenting a forecast as a certain business outcome')
monitor=m('Monitoring, responsible use & capstone review','shield','Show when a model is useful, when it should defer and when it needs review.','Data drift versus changes in predictive performance|Monitoring when labels arrive late|Subgroup error analysis and limitations of small samples|Human review, inappropriate uses and sensitive data minimisation|Model cards, reproducibility and retraining approval','pandas — compare input distributions and labelled outcomes|Python monitoring scripts — generate a small review report|Git and a model-card template — version assumptions and intended use','Simulate a change in input distribution and a rise in error once labels arrive. Prepare a review recommendation and a human fallback; do not automate retraining simply because a drift score changed.','Model card with intended use and exclusions|Monitoring report with alert rationale|Capstone review package and reproducibility instructions','Distinguish a drift signal from evidence of model failure|State sample-size limitations when comparing groups|Document who decides whether to retain, revise or retire the model')
d['modules']=[old[0],old[1],features,old[2],models,old[3],time,old[4],old[5],monitor];save('extended-programs/ml',d)
d=json.loads((base/'extended-programs/fullstack.json').read_text());old=d['modules']
ui=m('Interface design, accessibility & responsive layouts','layers','Build interfaces people can understand and operate across devices.','Semantic HTML and meaningful page structure|Responsive grids, typography and content hierarchy|Labels, validation messages, keyboard focus and status feedback|Loading, empty, success and failure states|Reusable components and design tokens','HTML and CSS — create resilient responsive layouts|Browser accessibility tools — inspect names, roles and focus|Angular templates — connect component state to clear feedback','Design a course-search and application flow at mobile and desktop widths. Include an empty result, invalid form, slow request and successful submission without relying on colour alone.','Responsive interface and reusable component inventory|Keyboard walkthrough notes|Documented loading, empty and error states','Complete the core task with a keyboard|Keep text and controls usable at 320 pixels|Preserve entered values after recoverable validation errors')
asyncm=m('State, asynchronous flows & client performance','network','Keep the screen consistent when requests are slow, repeated or cancelled.','Component state, shared state and clear ownership|Signals and observable streams in Angular|Debounced search and cancelling obsolete requests|Route loading, caching boundaries and stale data|Profiling rendering, bundle size and network requests','Angular signals — model local and shared reactive state|RxJS — compose and cancel asynchronous streams|Browser performance and network panels — inspect bottlenecks','Build searchable paginated results with loading feedback. Delay responses so older requests finish last and verify that the latest search still controls the screen.','Search and pagination implementation|State ownership diagram|Before-and-after performance observations','Prevent stale responses from replacing newer results|Clean up subscriptions and repeated event handlers|Explain caching choices and invalidation behaviour')
data=m('Data modelling, queries & consistency','database','Choose data structures around real reads, updates and constraints.','MongoDB embedding versus references|Schema validation, indexes and query inspection|Pagination and bounded result sets|Atomic updates, transaction boundaries and repeated requests|Relational modelling and migrations in the Python backend path','MongoDB — model document relationships and inspect queries|MongoDB Compass — explore sample data and indexes|PostgreSQL — compare relational constraints in the Python stream','Model users, projects and applications for a sample opportunities portal. Compare two document designs, add an index for a frequent query and handle a repeated application safely.','Data model and example access patterns|Index rationale and query evidence|Duplicate-request and constraint tests','Tie each index to an actual query|Avoid unbounded data reads and growing embedded arrays|Explain which consistency guarantees the chosen operation provides')
security=m('Authentication, authorisation & integration boundaries','shield','Connect accounts and external services without trusting the browser.','Authentication versus permission to act|Sessions, cookies and token lifecycle concepts|Object-level access checks and role boundaries|Input validation, output handling and safe database queries|External API timeouts, retries and server-side configuration','Express middleware — enforce permissions on server routes|FastAPI dependencies — illustrate equivalent checks in the Python path|A test identity provider or fixtures — practise login without real credentials|HTTP test clients — exercise unauthorised and repeated requests','Add member and reviewer roles to a sample request workflow. Attempt to access another user’s record, replay a request and call an unavailable service; make the server enforce each boundary.','Permission matrix and protected routes|Negative tests for cross-user access|Integration error and retry policy','Treat hidden UI controls as convenience, not authorisation|Keep secrets out of bundles and version control|Avoid duplicate side effects during retry')
d['modules']=[old[0],ui,old[1],asyncm,old[2],old[3],data,security,old[4],old[5]];save('extended-programs/fullstack',d)
d=json.loads((base/'extended-programs/leadership.json').read_text());old=d['modules']
discovery=m('Workflow discovery & opportunity framing','search','Start with a business process and a measurable problem.','Current-state workflow and handoff mapping|Customer, employee and operator perspectives|Task suitability: deterministic software, assistance or bounded automation|Baseline measures and counterfactual questions|Choosing a pilot with a manageable impact boundary','Workflow canvas — map tasks, decisions and exceptions|Interview guide — collect observations rather than solution preferences|Opportunity scorecard — compare value, readiness and uncertainty','Review an illustrative invoice-query workflow. Identify the real delay, interview questions, non-AI alternatives and the smallest useful pilot boundary.','Current-state map and problem statement|Baseline measurement plan|Opportunity shortlist with explicit assumptions','Connect the proposed capability to an observed problem|Consider simpler process or software changes|Make unresolved assumptions visible before funding')
data=m('Data readiness & architecture choices','database','Ask the questions that connect a proposal to the organisation’s systems.','Source ownership, access rights and information quality|Retrieval, model adaptation and system integration at a decision level|Identity, permissions and auditability|Vendor dependencies, portability and exit planning|Human review points and failure containment','Architecture canvas — explain systems and trust boundaries|Data-readiness checklist — identify ownership and quality gaps|Build–buy–partner matrix — compare operating responsibilities','Compare a document assistant delivered as a managed service with an internal application. Identify who owns access, corrections, evaluations and the ongoing service.','One-page architecture with trust boundaries|Data-readiness gap list and owners|Option comparison with exit assumptions','Distinguish product claims from evidence available for review|Identify an owner for each data source and access decision|Include ongoing operations when comparing options')
assurance=m('Evaluation, assurance & decision gates','check','Define the evidence a pilot must produce before it expands.','Task quality, unsupported answers and consequential errors|Representative test sets and adversarial scenarios|Human review effort, latency and total service cost|Pilot gates, acceptance criteria and stop conditions|Independent challenge and escalation responsibilities','Evaluation scorecard — relate evidence to intended use|Scenario library — test ordinary cases and important failures|Decision log — record proceed, revise and pause reasoning','Inspect a sample AI pilot scorecard with strong average results but poor handling of high-impact exceptions. Decide what evidence is missing and whether the scope should change.','Acceptance scorecard and review plan|Pilot gate decision with conditions|Escalation and exception ownership map','Do not substitute a demo or single metric for acceptance evidence|Define thresholds before reviewing pilot results|Account for human work needed to operate safely')
adoption=m('Adoption, operating model & stakeholder communication','users','Prepare people and responsibilities alongside the technology.','Process redesign and new ownership responsibilities|Role-based enablement and user feedback|Adoption measures versus business outcomes|Procurement and implementation handovers|Executive updates that separate facts, assumptions and decisions','Responsibility matrix — clarify who decides and operates|Adoption plan — sequence enablement and feedback|Executive update template — present evidence and requested decisions','Prepare a rollout conversation for business users, engineering, security and support. Explain changed responsibilities, the fallback process and how feedback will change the pilot.','Stakeholder map and responsibility matrix|Enablement and feedback plan|Executive update and handover checklist','Name accountable owners rather than generic teams alone|Measure actual use and task outcomes separately|Keep open risks and remaining decisions visible')
d['modules']=[old[0],discovery,data,old[1],assurance,old[2],adoption,old[3]];save('extended-programs/leadership',d)
d=json.loads((base/'space.json').read_text());old=d['modules']
mission=m('Orbit, coverage & mission analysis','orbit','Connect an observation objective to an explicit mission model.','Orbital elements and circular-orbit approximations|Ground tracks, coverage and revisit tradeoffs|Eclipse and contact-window assumptions|Sensitivity to altitude and mission constraints|Units, reference frames and model limitations','Python and NumPy — calculate and compare assumptions|Jupyter and Matplotlib — visualise orbital scenarios|GMAT or an equivalent teaching simulator — inspect a configured mission model','Compare two illustrative mission concepts for monitoring an area. Estimate period, examine simulated coverage and document which conclusions the simplified model cannot support.','Mission comparison notebook|Ground-track or coverage visualisation|Assumption and sensitivity register','Keep period, coverage and revisit distinct|Label units and reference-frame assumptions|Present simulator output with its configuration and limitations')
mechanical=m('Structures, thermal thinking & payload interfaces','wrench','Bring mechanical and electronics decisions into one reviewable design.','Mechanical envelope, mass properties and access for assembly|Payload mounting and connector clearances|Conduction, radiation and simple thermal balances|Material choices, tolerances and environmental assumptions|Interface documentation and change control','FreeCAD or equivalent CAD — model an educational assembly|Python spreadsheets or notebooks — track mass and thermal assumptions|Interface-control template — agree mechanical and electrical boundaries','Create a non-flight educational payload enclosure and interface drawing. Track mass, connector access and a simple thermal scenario; review a design change with another subsystem team.','CAD concept and annotated interface drawing|Mass budget and thermal assumptions|Design-change review record','Identify model simplifications and unverified loads|Show how the assembly can be connected and inspected|Do not describe the model as flight-qualified hardware')
software=m('Flight-software concepts & fault management','cpu','Make state, timing and recovery visible in a simulated controller.','Boot, nominal, safe and recovery states|Sensor sampling, command validation and telemetry queues|Watchdogs, timeout handling and resource limits|Fault detection, isolation and recovery concepts|Repeatable simulation and software verification','Python state-machine simulator — explore control logic|pytest — automate fault and recovery cases|Microcontroller tooling — optional supervised ground-hardware extension','Build a simulated subsystem controller. Inject a missing sensor, delayed command and restart; demonstrate how the controller enters a safe state and reports the reason.','State diagram and controller simulation|Fault-injection test suite|Recovery and event-log evidence','Define safe-state entry and exit conditions explicitly|Reject malformed or out-of-sequence commands|Keep recovery bounded and observable')
ops=m('Ground operations, telemetry review & verification','radio','Show how a team will operate and review the demonstrator.','Telemetry schemas, timestamps and engineering units|Command approval, acknowledgements and stale data|Contact planning and simulated link loss|Verification matrices and acceptance evidence|Operations procedures and anomaly handover','Python and Plotly — inspect replayed telemetry|CSV or SQLite — retain sample telemetry with schema metadata|Git — version procedures and verification evidence','Run a simulated ground-operations rehearsal. Replay a telemetry stream, lose contact, recover state and hand the next operator a clear account of what happened.','Ground dashboard and replay dataset|Verification matrix with pass/fail evidence|Operations runbook and anomaly report','Clearly distinguish live, replayed and stale data|Trace each requirement to a test result|Keep all radio work simulated unless facilities and approvals are separately agreed')
d['modules']=[old[0],mission,old[1],mechanical,old[2],software,ops,old[3]]
for i,x in enumerate(d['modules']):x.setdefault('icon',['satellite','orbit','battery','wrench','radio','cpu','chart','compass'][i])
save('space',d)
print('Expanded curricula: ML 10, Full-stack 10, Leaders 8, Space 8.')
